{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-15_12-22-18-hashicorp_raft-real-run/draft && python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nst=json.load(open('../state.json'))\ncur=[i for i in st['interpretations'] if i.get('id')=='0c18dc2523f14459925e467d38fe022f-interpretation-0'][0]\nV5=\\\"be69cdfff5274bc391795508e987429d\\\"\nIDX=[1,7,13,25,27,29,3,9,15,5,11,17,19]\nlim=[l for l in cur['limitations'] if not l.startswith('The batched cases use the default MaxAppendEntries')]\nlim.append(\\\"The over-subscribed cases carry 320 concurrent racing calls, five times the 64 verifyCh slots, so a large share of sends could not be accepted; the buffer still ended with free slots and the strand persisted, which means occupancy at the exit is not what the probe controls.\\\")\ninterp={\n \\\"investigation_id\\\":\\\"b2ccc787c9384b008b5f9c668746f760-question-0\\\",\n \\\"experiment_id\\\":\\\"4916079656954a2b81e3a6bfdb12f816-experiment\\\",\n \\\"source_ids\\\":cur['source_ids'],\n \\\"executions\\\":{cur['executions'] and list(cur['executions'])[0]:cur['executions'][list(cur['executions'])[0]], V5:IDX},\n \\\"conclusion\\\":\\\"explained\\\",\n \\\"defect_claim\\\":\\\"asserted\\\",\n \\\"rationale\\\":(cur['rationale']+\\\" \\\"\n  \\\"A fifth revision tested whether the strand depends on spare capacity in verifyCh by issuing 320 concurrent racing calls, five times the 64 slots, in three VerifyLeader cases (result events at parsed indices 25, 27 and 29). Over-subscription did not protect later callers: 6, 5 and 6 of the eight post-shutdown calls were answered and 2, 3 and 2 returned futures that stayed incomplete, which is the same outcome as the 128-call cases in the same run (5, 1 and 3 answered; 3, 7 and 5 stranded) and the declared comparison asking for every post-shutdown call to be answered was therefore contradicted with three valid witnesses. The reading is that the racing surplus senders are released by the shutdown case instead of holding slots, so the buffer ends partially empty at the exit and later callers still find a free slot to be accepted into; occupancy at the exit is thus not what decides the strand, and the mechanism stands as the buffered channel plus a future with no shutdown channel of its own.\\\"),\n \\\"knowledge\\\":cur['knowledge'],\n \\\"answers\\\":{},\n \\\"counterevidence\\\":cur['counterevidence']+[\n  \\\"Over-subscribing verifyCh five-fold did not remove the strand: the 320-call cases stranded 2, 3 and 2 of eight post-shutdown calls, against 3, 7 and 5 of eight for the 128-call cases, so the outcome is not decided by spare capacity being available when the loop exits.\\\"],\n \\\"limitations\\\":lim,\n \\\"joint_history\\\":cur['joint_history']+\\\" The fifth revision 4916079656954a2b81e3a6bfdb12f816-experiment reuses the same harness, adds over-subscribed VerifyLeader cases and takes the call count as a parameter; event names, case kinds and field meanings are unchanged, so its racing and post-shutdown fields are comparable with the earlier revisions.\\\"}\nknowledge={\n \\\"id\\\":\\\"c27ce810268e4535bf01c8870a682db4-knowledge-0\\\",\n \\\"kind\\\":\\\"fact\\\",\n \\\"statement\\\":(\\\"VerifyLeader can hand back a future that nothing will ever complete, because the request waits in the buffered verifyCh that no reader drains once the run loop has exited and the future itself carries no shutdown channel to unblock on. The trigger does not require racing Shutdown: calls made after Shutdown has already returned strand about half the time. The corrected revision measured 11 of 24 post-shutdown VerifyLeader calls stranded against 0 of 48 for the default unbuffered Barrier and Apply, and with BatchApplyCh - which buffers applyCh - Barrier stranded 11 of 24 and Apply 13 of 24. A later revision over-subscribed verifyCh with 320 concurrent racing calls, five times its 64 slots, and the strand persisted (2, 3 and 2 of eight post-shutdown calls incomplete), so spare capacity at the exit is not what decides it: the surplus senders are released by the shutdown case rather than holding slots.\\\"),\n \\\"conditions\\\":\\\"Single-voter Raft instance, HeartbeatTimeout = ElectionTimeout = LeaderLeaseTimeout = 50ms, in-memory transport in one process, BatchApplyCh off unless stated; 128 or 320 concurrent calls around Shutdown plus eight sequential calls after Shutdown has returned.\\\",\n \\\"source_ids\\\":cur['source_ids'],\n \\\"executions\\\":{\\\"b0748389f0ab44d89142c25404fe247c\\\":[1,7,13,25,27,29,33,35,3,9,15,5,11,17], V5:[1,7,13,25,27,29,19]},\n \\\"changed_premise\\\":(\\\"The premise is unchanged and one proposed explanation is removed: the strand is not conditional on spare capacity in the buffered channel, since over-subscribing it five-fold left the outcome unchanged. The earlier counts stay and the over-subscribed ones are added.\\\"),\n \\\"affected_uses\\\":[]}\nd={\\\"rationale\\\":(\\\"Interpreted the over-subscription revision, which refutes the occupancy explanation rather than the defect: with 320 racing calls against 64 slots the post-shutdown strand persisted (2, 3 and 2 of eight calls incomplete), so the buffer is not full when the loop exits and later callers still find a free slot. The account keeps its defect claim and its earlier counts, gains that counterevidence item and a corrected limitation, and the Fact is extended under its own id to record that spare capacity is not the deciding factor. No execution is requested.\\\"),\n \\\"knowledge\\\":[knowledge],\n \\\"interpretations\\\":[interp]}\njson.dump(d,open('update.json','w'),indent=2,ensure_ascii=False); open('update.json','a').write('\\\\n')\nPY\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-15_12-22-18-hashicorp_raft-real-run --submission update.json 2>&1 | tail -2\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
